From c639cbeed31ec34c4ed32c8edeefa5aa1dc5b793 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <hank@quorra.ah.local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:36:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 26/58] dsv4 indexer: tile the dense fp4 prefill scoring over
 query rows under the score budget (recipe E34b)

_low_ratio_index_topk_dense scored a whole prefill chunk in one [rows, width] fp32
logits tensor (4 B x prefix per row: 1 GiB at 64K, 1.75 GiB at 110K), which OOMed the
128K ladder step. Every kernel on the path (fp8_fp4_mqa_logits, select_candidate_blocks,
topk_transform_ragged_v2, _mask_topk_scores) is per query row, so _dense_index_topk_rows
walks the rows in tiles whose logits fit _TORCH_INDEXER_SCORE_BUDGET_BYTES (the bound the
torch path already uses), publishing / consuming candidate masks per request segment
inside each tile. Bit-exact vs the single-tile path (recipe
scripts/tests/test_indexer_row_tiling.py: logits identical, top-k sets identical; the
fused top-k's intra-row order is launch-shape dependent and the caller sorts).

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0c10b-a5f8-77fc-b238-7147d12ccf29
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
